 "result": "**Where to look**\n- `src/tessel/sessions.py:304-312`: the session serializer signs with `app.secret_key` and also accepts old keys from `SECRET_KEY_HISTORY`.\n- `src/tessel/app.py:210-211`: the config defaults, where both are `None`.\n- `docs/config.rst:114-141`: documents both settings.\n\n**How to rotate without logging everyone out**\n\nMove the old key into `SECRET_KEY_HISTORY` and set the new one as `SECRET_KEY`:\n\n```python\nSECRET_KEY = \"<new key>\"\nSECRET_KEY_HISTORY = [\"<old key>\"]\n```\n\nExisting sessions then still validate against the old key. They get re-signed with the new key the next time they're saved. Once the old sessions have expired (after `PERMANENT_SESSION_LIFETIME`), remove the old key from the list.\n\nTwo caveats:\n- `docs/config.rst:141` says extensions that use `SECRET_KEY` directly may not support the history list yet. Anything those extensions sign (CSRF tokens, for example) can still be invalidated.\n- Make sure the history list is set in every process and instance before you roll out the new key, or some will reject the old sessions.",
